export const aoaTemplateRaw = "\n\n**Articles of Association** \n\n**Swiss Association**\n\n**Description:** \n\nMain Governing Document of the Swiss Association. Set of procedures to setup and run the entity. It should be used with the Regulation of General Assembly and the [Inaugural Meeting Minutes](https://docs.google.com/document/d/12mBUqRvg_000_O77jSFDeF9rPBWytAAe/edit).\n\n**Variable Parameters**:\n\n* *“Signatory”: Signing Party (Name, Company)*  \n  * *“Association Name”: Legal title of your association*  \n  * *“Purpose”: Non-profit purpose of your association*  \n  * *“Date”: Execution Date*\n\n**Fix Parameters**\n\n* Address \\[MJP domicile provider\\]\n\n|  |  |  |  |\n| ----- | ----- | ----- | ----- |\n|  |  |  |  |\n| **\\[Association Name\\] Vereinsstatuten** | **\\[Association Name\\] Articles of Association** |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |\n| ***Name*** | ***Name*** |  |  |\n| Unter dem Namen “ \\[Association Name\\]” besteht ein gemeinnütziger Verein im Sinne der Artikel 60 bis 79 des Schweizerischen Zivilgesetzbuches. Dieser Verein ist eine selbständige juristische Person mit eigener Rechtspersönlichkeit. Er untersteht schweizerischem Recht. Seine Dauer ist unbegrenzt.  | A non-profit association named “\\[Association Name\\]” (the “**Association**”) is hereby established pursuant to Articles 60 to 79 of the Swiss Civil Code. The Association is an independent legal entity with legal capacity. It is governed by Swiss law. Its duration is unlimited.   |  |  |\n| Die offizielle Sprache des Vereins ist Englisch. | The official language of the association is English. |  |  |\n| ***Sitz*** | ***Registered Office*** |  |  |\n| Der Verein hat seinen Sitz und seine Verwaltung in Zug, Schweiz. Der Verein kann auch Niederlassungen an anderen Orten haben. | The Association shall establish and maintain a registered office and administration in \\[Address\\] Zug, Switzerland. The Association may also have offices in other locations. |  |  |\n| ***Zweck*** | ***Purpose*** |  |  |\n| Der Zweck des Vereins, eine nicht gewinnorientierte Organisation, ist, die Zusammenarbeit zu orchestrieren und Teams zu unterstützen, die technologische öffentliche Güter herstellen. | The purpose of the Association, a non-profit organisation, is to \\[purpose\\] |  |  |\n| Der Verein kann allgemein zur Verwirklichung des vorgenannten Zwecks notwendige und geeignete Massnahmen ergreifen sowie Initiativen planen und durchführen und sich \\- auch nur finanziell \\- an Initiativen anderer Organisationen beteiligen oder andere Organisationen oder Personen finanziell oder anderweitig unterstützen, soweit alle diese Aktivitäten dem Vereinszweck dienen. Der Verein kann auch Spenden von Dritten annehmen und zur Verfolgung seines Zwecks treuhänderisch tätig werden. Der Verein verfolgt keine kommerziellen Zwecke und strebt keinen Gewinn an. | The Association may generally take necessary and appropriate measures to implement the above-mentioned purpose as well as plan and implement initiatives and – even only financially – participate in initiatives of other organizations or support financially or otherwise other organizations or individuals to the extent that all such activities serve the purpose of the Association. The Association may also accept donations from third persons and act as fiduciary to pursue its purpose. The Association does not pursue commercial purposes and does not strive for profit. |  |  |\n| ***Mitgliedschaft*** | ***Membership*** |  |  |\n| ***4.1 Gründungsmitglieder und Mitglieder*** | ***4.1 Members*** |  |  |\n| Der Verein ist offen für jede natürliche Person, die für sich selbst handelt oder die eine von der Generalversammlung definierte Gesellschaftsform ohne Rechtspersönlichkeit vertritt, jede Kapitalgesellschaft, Personengesellschaft, Verein, Trust, öffentliche oder private gemeinnützige Forschungseinrichtung, staatliche Stelle, oder andere juristische Person (\"**Mitglieder**\"), die den Zweck des Vereins unterstützt, ein Interesse daran hat, sich an den Aktivitäten des Vereins zu beteiligen, und die von der Generalversammlung definierten Mitgliedschaftskriterien (“**Mitgliedschaftskriterien**”) erfüllt.  | The Association is open to membership by any natural person acting for himself or herself or representing an unincorporated entity as defined by the General Assembly, any corporation, partnership, association, trust, public or private non-profit research institution, governmental body, or other legal entity (\"**Members**\") that supports the purpose of the Association, and fulfils the membership criteria (“**Membership Criteria**”) defined by the General Assembly. |  |  |\n| ***4.2 Mitgliedschaftsbeitrag*** | ***4.2 Membership Fee*** |  |  |\n| Der jährliche Mitgliederbeitrag wird durch die Generalversammlung festgelegt. Die Generalversammlung kann auf die Erhebung von Mitgliederbeiträgen verzichten. | The annual membership fee is determined by the General Assembly. The General Assembly may waive the collection of membership fees. |  |  |\n| ***4.3 Aufnahme*** | ***4.3 Admission*** |  |  |\n| Aufnahmeanträge müssen an die Generalversammlung gerichtet und von ihr geprüft werden.  | Applications for admission must be submitted to and assessed by the General Assembly. |  |  |\n| ***4.4  Ende der Mitgliedschaft und Ausschluss*** | ***4.4 End of Membership and Expulsion*** |  |  |\n| Mitglieder können jederzeit aus dem Verein austreten, wenn sie dies der Generalversammlung (Briefpost, E-Mail oder eine andere von der Vereinsversammlung bestimmte und jedem Mitglied schriftlich mitgeteilte Kommunikationsmethode) mitteilen. | Members may resign from the Association at any time, provided that they notify the General Assembly (mail, e-mail, or any other method of communication as determined and notified to each Member in writing by the General Assembly).  |  |  |\n| Die Mitglieder treten automatisch aus dem Verein aus bzw. die Mitgliedschaft erlischt, wenn die Mitgliedschaftskriterien nicht mehr erfüllt sind. | Members automatically resign from the Association/the membership lapses (*Erlöschen der Mitgliedschaft*) when the Membership Criteria are no longer met. |  |  |\n| Jedes Mitglied hat die Einhaltung der Mitgliedschaftskriterien laufend zu prüfen. Jedes Mitglied, das feststellt, dass es eines oder mehrere der Mitgliedschaftskriterien nicht mehr erfüllt, muss unverzüglich (und innerhalb von höchstens fünf Arbeitstagen) als Mitglied zurücktreten, indem es die Generalversammlung benachrichtigt. | Each Member shall diligently monitor compliance with the Membership Criteria. Any Member who becomes aware of ceasing to satisfy any one or more of the Membership Criteria shall promptly (and in no less than five business days) unconditionally resign as an Member by notifying the General Assembly. |  |  |\n| Die Generalversammlung kann ein Mitglied durch eine schriftliche Mitteilung ausschliessen, wenn in jedem einzelnen Fall (a) es gegen diese Statuten oder eine Regelung des Vereins verstösst, (b) das Vereinsmitglied Betrug, vorsätzliches Fehlverhalten, grobe Fahrlässigkeit, einen vorsätzlichen und wissentlichen Verstoss gegen diese Statuten oder ein Reglement oder ein Verbrechen mit moralischer Verwerflichkeit begangen hat oder mit hoher Wahrscheinlichkeit beging, (c) einer rechtskräftigen, unanfechtbaren (oder nicht zu erwartenden) Verfügung eines zuständigen Gerichts oder einer Aufsichtsbehörde, die den Ausschluss eines Mitglieds anordnet oder die Aktivitäten des Mitglieds in Verbindung mit dem Verein wesentlich einschränkt; (d) das Mitglied erfüllt die Mitgliedschaftskriterien nicht mehr, (e) eine Bedingung eingetreten ist, durch welche die Fortsetzung der Mitgliedschaft des Mitglieds wesentliche nachteilige Auswirkung auf den Vereins hat, oder (f) ein Verhalten an den Tag gelegt hat, das den Interessen des Vereins schadet.  | The General Assembly may expel a Member by written notice in each case a Member has (a) breached the Articles or any regulation of the Association, (b) committed, or demonstrated a high likelihood to commit, fraud, willful misconduct, gross negligence, an intentional and knowing breach of these Articles or any applicable regulation, or a crime involving moral turpitude; (c) incurred any final, non-appealable (or not reasonably expected to be appealed) order of any court of competent jurisdiction or regulatory authority ordering the removal of the Member or materially limiting the Member’s activities in connection with the Association; (d) lost eligibility under the Membership Criteria or (e) entered a condition such that the Member’s continued membership in the Association would have a continuing material adverse effect on the Association, or (f) engaged in behavior detrimental to the interests of the Association.   |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |\n| Austretende oder ausgeschlossene Mitglieder haben keinen Anspruch auf bereits bezahlte Mitgliederbeiträge.  | Resigning or expelled Members do not receive a refund for any membership fees paid.  |  |  |\n| Die Teilnahme- und Stimmrechte der ausgetretenen oder ausgeschlossenen Mitglieder enden mit der Austrittserklärung bzw. dem Beschluss über den Ausschluss.  | The participation and voting rights of resigned or expelled Members ceases at time of their resignation respectively or expulsion. |  |  |\n| Ausgeschiedene oder ausgeschlossene Mitglieder haben keine Ansprüche am Vermögen des Vereins. Jede Verpflichtung eines austretenden oder ausgeschlossenen Mitglieds in diesen Statuten oder in anderen Organisationsdokumenten des Vereins, die ausdrücklich oder aufgrund ihrer Natur den Austritt oder den Ausschluss von der Mitgliedschaft überdauern sollen, gelten auch nach dem Austritt oder Ausschluss von der Mitgliedschaft weiter. | Resigning or excluded Members have no rights against the assets of the Association. Any obligation of a resigning or excluded Member in these Articles or other Organizational Documents of the Association which, explicitly or by its nature, should survive resignation or expulsion of membership, will survive any such resignation or expulsion of membership. |  |  |\n| ***Organe*** | ***Bodies*** |  |  |\n| Die Organe des Vereins sind: die Generalversammlung (Personalunion mit Vorstand); andere Organe, falls von der Generalversammlung bestimmt und in den Statuten oder Reglementen festgelegt; und die Revisionsstelle (falls von der Generalversammlung bestimmt oder eine gesetzliche Pflicht besteht). | The bodies of the Association are: the General Assembly (personal union with the board); other bodies if determined by the General Assembly and established in the Articles of Association or regulations; and the auditors (if elected by the General Assembly or required by law). |  |  |\n| ***Generalversammlung*** | ***General Assembly*** |  |  |\n| ***6.1 Befugnisse*** | ***6.1 Powers*** |  |  |\n| Die Generalversammlung hat die folgenden Befugnisse: die Annahme und Änderung der Statuten und der Reglemente; die Wahl der Mitglieder anderer Organe (sofern vorhanden); Wahl des Vorsitzenden der Generalversammlung; die Abberufung von Mitgliedern von Organen, sofern ein Mitglied (i) gegen diese Statuten oder gegen eine Regelung des Vereins verstösst oder (ii) ein Verhalten an den Tag legt, das den Interessen des Vereins zuwiderläuft; die Bestellung der Revisionsstelle, sofern ein entsprechender Antrag von einem Mitglied gestellt wird oder eine solche Bestellung gesetzlich vorgeschrieben ist; die Genehmigung der Jahresrechnung des Vereins sowie des Berichts der Revisionsstelle (falls vorhanden); den Verein zu leiten und zu verwalten sowie alle Aufgaben und Befugnisse wahrzunehmen, die dem Vorstand (Personalunion) allgemein durch geltendes Recht oder die Statuten unter zugewiesen sind. die Aufsicht und die Gewährung der Entlastung für die Mitglieder der Organe; weitere in den Statuten oder den Reglementen der Generalversammlung zugewiesene Befugnisse. | The General Assembly has the following powers: to adopt and amend the Articles of Association and any regulations; to elect the members of other bodies (if any);  to elect the chair of the General Assembly; to dismiss members of bodies if a member of a body is (i) in breach of these articles of association or any regulation of the Association or (ii) engaging in behavior detrimental to the interests of the Association;  to appoint an auditor provided that a corresponding motion has been presented by a Member or if such appointment is required by law; to approve the financial statements of the Association as well as any audit report (if available); to supervise and grant discharge to the members of the bodies; to operate and manage the Association as well as perform all duties and powers generally assigned to the board (*Personalunion*) by applicable law or the Articles. other powers assigned to the General Assembly in the Articles of Association or the regulations.  |  |  |\n| ***6.2 Arten der Generalversammlung und Beschlussfassung durch schriftliche/elektronische Kommunikation (Urabstimmung)*** | ***6.2 Alternatives for the General Assembly and resolutions by means of written/electronic communication (\"Urabstimmung\")*** |  |  |\n| Die Generalversammlung kann virtuell (Telefon- oder Videokonferenz) oder physisch abgehalten werden. Es kann auch eine gemischte physische und virtuelle Generalversammlung stattfinden, bei der die Mitglieder frei entscheiden, ob sie physisch präsent sein möchten oder virtuell teilnehmen möchten. | The General Assembly may be held as a virtual (telephone or video conference) or physical meeting. It is possible to hold the General Assembly as a mixed physical and virtual meeting, in which Members decide whether to participate physically or virtually. |  |  |\n| Die Mitglieder können bestimmen, dass über sämtliche traktandierten Geschäfte (einschliesslich Wahlen) mittels schriftlicher / elektronischer Kommunikation (\"Urabstimmung\") abgestimmt wird (per Briefpost, E-Mail oder eine andere von der Generalversammlung bestimmte Kommunikationsmethode), in welchem Fall die Mitglieder entsprechend über die Ergebnisse informiert werden sollen.  | The Members may determine that all agenda items (including elections) shall be voted on by means of written / electronic communication (by mail, e-mail, or any other method of communication as determined by the General Assembly) (*Urabstimmung*), in which case all Members shall be informed of results.  |  |  |\n| ***6.3 Organisation der Generalversammlung*** | ***6.3 Organization of the General Assembly*** |  |  |\n| Die Organisation der Generalversammlung in Bezug auf die Einberufung, die Beschlussfassung, die Stimmrechte und die Mehrheiten sind in einem oder mehreren durch die Generalversammlung angenommenen Reglementen festgelegt (”**Reglement Generalversammlung**”).  | The organization of the General Assembly regarding convening, passing resolutions, voting rights and majorities are laid down in one or more regulations adopted by the General Assembly (\"**Regulation General Assembly**\"). |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |\n| ***6.4 Schadloshaltung*** | ***6.4 Indemnification*** |  |  |\n| Jedes Mitglied des Vorstands, der Präsident der Geschäftsleitung, jeder Geschäftsführer, jede Person, die gegenwärtig oder früher in dieser Eigenschaft tätig war, und ihre persönlichen Vertreter (jeweils eine \"**schadloszuhaltende Person**\") haben Anspruch darauf, vom Verein für alle Handlungen, Verfahren, Kosten, Schäden, Ausgaben, Ansprüche, Verluste, Verbindlichkeiten, Geldbussen oder Beträge, die aufgrund von Handlungen oder Unterlassungen bei der Ausübung ihrer jeweiligen Ämter oder in sonstiger Weise in diesem Zusammenhang entstanden sind oder drohen, einschliesslich der Kostenvorschüsse, die bei der Verteidigung in zivil- oder strafrechtlichen Verfahren anfallen, schadlos gehalten zu werden, es sei denn, das Vorgenannte ist auf grobe Fahrlässigkeit oder vorsätzliches Fehlverhalten der schadloszuhaltenden Person zurückzuführen. | Every Board member, President of the Management, executive director, any individual currently or formerly acting in such capacity and their personal representatives (each an \"**Indemnified Person**\") shall be entitled to be indemnified by the Association against all actions, proceedings, costs, damages, expenses, claims, losses, liabilities, fines or amounts made or threatened by reason of any act done or omitted in or about the execution of the duties of their respective offices or otherwise in relation thereto, including any advances of expenses to be incurred in defending any proceedings, whether civil or criminal, except to the extent that any of the foregoing arise through the Indemnified Person’s gross negligence or willful misconduct.  |  |  |\n| ***Rechnungslegung, Buchhaltung und Belege*** | ***Accounting, Books and Records*** |  |  |\n| Der Verein führt die erforderliche Buchhaltung und Belege. | The Association shall maintain books and records as appropriate.  |  |  |\n| Das Rechnungslegungsjahr und das Geschäftsjahr des Vereins laufen vom 1\\. Januar bis zum 31\\. Dezember. Der Generalversammlung kann nach eigenem Ermessen ein überlanges Geschäftsjähr festlegen. | The accounting and fiscal year of the Association shall run from January 1 to December 31\\. The General Assembly may, at its own discretion, determine an extra-long association year. |  |  |\n| ***Finanzierung*** | ***Finance*** |  |  |\n| Die finanziellen Mittel des Vereins bestehen aus: Geld;  Kryptographische Token; Digitale Vermögenswerte, die in den Verein eingebracht werden oder sich anderweitig im Rahmen der Geschäftstätigkeit im Besitz des Vereins befinden;  Mitgliedsbeiträge (falls vorhanden); Finanzierungsinitiativen, Beiträge (einschliesslich Spenden und Vermächtnisse); Subventionen von öffentlichen Behörden oder anderen Organisationen; und/oder sonstige Vermögenswerte, welche die Generalversammlung nach eigenem Ermessen festlegt und die gesetzlich zulässig sind. | The financial resources of the Association shall consist of: Cash;  Cryptographic tokens;  Digital assets contributed to or otherwise held by the Association in the course of its normal operations;  Membership fees (if any); fundraising initiatives, contributions (incl. donations and legacies); subsidies from public authorities or other organizations; and/or such other assets as determined by the General Assembly in its discretion and as permitted by law.  |  |  |\n| Die finanziellen Verpflichtungen des Vereins können nur aus dem Vereinsvermögen beglichen werden. Die Mitglieder des Vereins haften nicht persönlich für die Verpflichtungen oder Schulden des Vereins. | The Association’s financial obligations can be satisfied only from its assets. The Members of the Association shall not be personally liable for the obligations or debts of the Association. |  |  |\n| ***Revisionsstelle (sofern bestellt)*** | ***Auditor (if appointed)*** |  |  |\n| Die Generalversammlung wählt eine juristische oder natürliche Person als Revisionsstelle des Vereins für ein Geschäftsjahr. | The General Assembly elects a legal entity or natural person as auditor of the Association for one financial year. |  |  |\n| Die Jahresrechnung ist jährlich zu erstellen. Die Revisionsstelle prüft jährlich die Konten, die Buchhaltung und Unterlagen des Vereins in Übereinstimmung mit dem schweizerischen Recht und ist berechtigt, die zur Erfüllung seiner Pflichten für notwendig und angemessen erachteten Nachweise zu verlangen. | The financial statements shall be prepared annually. The auditor shall annually audit the accounts, books and records of the Association in accordance with Swiss law, and shall be entitled to require such evidence as deemed necessary and appropriate to effectuate its duties.  |  |  |\n| Die Generalversammlung kann auf die Wahl einer Revisionsstelle verzichten, wenn der Verein in zwei aufeinander folgenden Geschäftsjahren zwei der folgenden Schwellenwerte nicht überschreitet: | The General Assembly may waive election of an Auditor if the Association does not exceed two of the following thresholds in two successive financial years: |  |  |\n| eine Bilanzsumme von 10 Millionen Franken; Umsatzerlöse von 20 Millionen Franken; 50 Vollzeitstellen im Jahresdurchschnitt. Dieser Verzicht gilt auch für die Folgejahre. vor. | a balance sheet total of 10 million francs; sales revenue of 20 million francs; 50 full-time positions on an annual average. This waiver also applies to the subsequent years. |  |  |\n| Die Revisionsstelle erstellt ihren Prüfungsbericht für das vorangegangene Kalenderjahr und legt ihn den Mitgliedern bis spätestens am 31\\. März eines jeden Kalenderjahres.   | The auditor shall prepare and deliver its audit report for the preceding calendar year to the Members no later than March 31 of each calendar year.   |  |  |\n| ***Auflösung und Liquidation*** | ***Dissolution and Liquidation*** |  |  |\n| Der Verein wird aufgelöst: wenn er seinen Zweck erfüllt hat;  durch Zustimmung aller Mitglieder; und/oder unter allen anderen Umständen, die vom Gesetz vorgesehen sind. | The Association shall be dissolved: when it has fulfilled its purposes;  through a unanimous vote of the Members ; and/or under any other circumstances required by applicable law.  |  |  |\n| Bei Auflösung wird der Verein das Vereinsvermögen liquidieren und sämtliche anderweitigen Handlungen für die Auflösung vornehmen. Die Schulden, Abgaben und sonstige Verpflichtungen sind zu begleichen. Verbleibendes Vermögen ist durch Beschluss der Generalversammlung entsprechend dem Vereinszweck zu verwenden und durch die Anerkennung einer solchen Verwendung durch die Steuerbehörden; eine Verteilung des bei der Auflösung verbleibenden Vermögens unter die Mitglieder, Personen oder Einrichtungen, die von einem Mitglied kontrolliert werden oder unter gemeinsamer Kontrolle mit einem Mitglied stehen ist ausgeschlossen. | Upon dissolution of the Association, the Association shall proceed to liquidate its assets and otherwise engage in appropriate actions to wind up its affairs. Debts, levies and other obligations must be paid. Any remaining assets shall be allocated in a manner consistent with the purpose of the Association by resolution of the General Assembly and by recognition of such use by the tax authorities; provided, however, that in no event shall Association assets be distributed to the Members, persons or entities controlled by or under common control with any Member, upon dissolution. |  |  |\n| ***Verhältnis der Statuten zum Gesetz*** |  | ***Relationship between Articles of Association and the law*** |  |\n| In Abweichung zu Artikel 63 (1) des Schweizerischen Zivilgesetzbuches gilt: Soweit die Statuten oder Reglemente des Vereins über die Organisation und über das Verhältnis des Vereins zu seinen Mitgliedern keine Vorschriften aufstellen, finden die Bestimmungen in Artikel 64 ff. Schweizerisches Zivilgesetzbuch Anwendung. |  | In derogation of article 63 (1) of the Swiss Civil Code, the following applies: where the articles of association or regulations of the association do not provide rules for the association’s organization or its relationship with its members, the provisions in article 64 et seq. Swiss Civil Code shall apply. |  |\n| ***Sprache*** |  | ***Language*** |  |\n| Der englische Text der vorliegenden Statuten ist massgebend. |  | The English version of these Articles of Association shall prevail. |  |\n| ***Inkrafttreten*** | ***Entry into Force*** |  |  |\n| Die Mitglieder haben die vorliegenden Statuten verabschiedet. Die vorliegenden Statuten sind heute in Kraft getreten. | The Members have adopted the present Articles of Association. The present Articles of Association have entered into force today. |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |\n\nZug, \\[Date\\], Switzerland\n\n\\[Signatories (Name, Company}\\]\n\n\\[cryptographic signature hash (per signing party, timestamp\\]\n\n---\n\n";

export const foundingMinutesTemplateRaw = "  \n**Founding Meeting Minutes**\n\n**Swiss Association**\n\n**Description:**   \nProtocolization of company incorporation\n\n**Variable Parameters**:\n\n* *“Signatory”: Signing Party (Name, Entity, Role)*  \n  * *Role (Chair, Secretary))*  \n* *Attendees \\= Founding members  (Name / Company \\+ representative, City)*  \n  * *\\+ MME rep*  \n* *“Association Name”: Legal title of your association*  \n* *“Date”: Execution Date*\n\n***Fix Parameters***\n\n* *Registered seat: Zug*  \n* *Meeting Place: Online*  \n* *Signatory power (by two)*\n\n**Founding Meeting  \\[Association Name\\]  \\- *Minutes*** \n\n*of the founding meeting of the Powerhouse Genesis Operational Hub association with registered seat in Zug* \n\n*\\[Date\\]* \n\n*Registered seat: Zug*\n\n*Place: Online*\n\n*Attendant* \n\n*Attendees (Name / Company \\+ representative, City)*\n\n*Attendees (Name / Company \\+ representative, City)*\n\n*Attendees (Name / Company \\+ representative, City)*\n\n \n\n*Chair \\[Role\\]*\n\n \n\n*Secretary  \\[Role\\]*\n\nAgenda \n\n1\\.*Formalities* \n\n2\\. *Founding decision* \n\n3\\. \n\n*Approval of the Articles of Association* \n\n4\\. *Adoption of the Regulation General Assembly* \n\n5\\. *Personal union* \n\n6\\. *Not required to register in the Commercial Register* \n\n7\\. *Election of the auditors* \n\n1\\. ***Formalities*** \n\n\\[Role, Chair\\] *is elected as chair and CARS as Secretary of the meeting*. \n\n**2.Founding decision** \n\n*The General Assembly resolves, under the name of \\[Association name\\] to*\n\n*establish an association in accordance with art*. *60 ff. of the Swiss Civil Code with registered seat in Zug*. \n\n**3\\. *Approval of the Articles of Association*** \n\n*The Assembly approves the present draft of the Articles of Association and defines them as the valid Articles of Association*. \n\n**4\\.*Adoption of the Regulation General Assembly*** \n\n*The Assembly approves the present draft of the Regulation General Assembly and defines it as the valid regulation of the association*. \n\n**5\\. *Personal union*** \n\n: *Due to the small number of members, the association does not have a separate board. The Assembly resolves that the administrative, executive, and representative functions assigned by law to the board are performed by all members as a self-governing body (see article 6 Articles of Association)*. *The members represent and sign for the Association as follows:* \n\n\t*\\[Attendees / Founding Members\\]*\n\n*with signatory power by \\[signatory power\\] by two* \n\n\t*\\[Attendees / Founding Members\\]*\n\n*with signatory power by *\n\n*\\[signatory power\\] by two* \n\n**6\\.**\n\n**Not *required to register in the Commercial Register*** \n\n*The Assembly notes that per January 1, 2023 according to article 61* (*2) CC associations in Switzerland are only required to register in the commercial register if the association (1) operates a business conducted in a commercial manner for its purpose, (2) is subject to auditing or (3) mainly collects or distributes assets abroad, directly or indirectly*, *intended for charitable religious, cultural, educational or social purposes*. \n\n*The Assembly acknowledges, resolves and confirms that the Association (1) does not self-finance its operation to fulfil its purpose by generating regular ongoing and high revenue through providing products or services against remuneration (operation of a business conducted in a commercial manner)*1 *and thus does not conducts a commercial operation in pursuit of its objects, (ii) it is not subject an audit requirement according to article 69b CC, and (iii) it does not does not directly or indirectly collect assets abroad that are not linked to a consideration (Gegenleistung) and thus does not primarily collect or distribute assets abroad, directly or indirectly, that are intended for charitable, religious, cultural*, *educational or social purpose Accordingly, the Association is not required to register in the commercial register according to article 61* (*2) CC.* \n\n*The Assembly will inform the competent commercial register and register if one of the requirements for the obligation to register according to article 61* (2*) CC are fulfilled in the future*. \n\n7\\. ***Election of the auditors*** \n\n*The Assembly renounces the election of an auditor*. \n\nAll *items have been dealt with.* \n\n. *After all agenda items have been dealt with, the chairperson closes the meeting*. \n\n*Chair* \n\n*Signatory”: Signing Party (Name, Entity, Role))*\n\n*Secretary* \n\n*“Signatory”: Signing Party (Name, Entity, Role))*\n\nAnnex: Articles of Association \n\nAnnex: Regulation General Assembly ";

export const contributorAgreementTemplateRaw = "# INDEPENDENT CONTRACTOR AGREEMENT\n\nThis Independent Contractor Agreement (“Agreement”) is entered into on [Contract Date]\nbetween:\n\n[Association Name], a Swiss Association duly organized in the canton of [Canton] with agent domiciled at [Registered Address] (hereinafter referred to as the “OH”).\n\nand\n\n<!-- BRANCH:ENTITY -->\n[Contractor Entity Name], a [Contractor Entity Type] duly organized in [Contractor Entity Jurisdiction] with agent domiciled at [Contractor Address] (hereinafter referred to as the “CONTRACTOR”).\n<!-- /BRANCH:ENTITY -->\n<!-- BRANCH:INDIVIDUAL -->\n[Contractor Name], a national of [Contractor Nationality] domiciled at [Contractor Address] (hereinafter referred to as the “CONTRACTOR”).\n<!-- /BRANCH:INDIVIDUAL -->\n\nThe parties above (the “Parties,” either being a “Party”) hereby agree as follows:\n\n## 1. SERVICES AND DELIVERABLES\n\nThe CONTRACTOR who is engaged as a Contractor shall perform the services (“Services”) for the OH, as set out in one or more statements of work to be issued by the OH, and accepted by the CONTRACTOR (each, a \"Statement of Work\"). The initial accepted Statement of Work is attached hereto as Schedule A, and subsequent Statements of Work, if any, shall be issued substantially in the same form.\n\n## 2. CONTRACTOR OBLIGATIONS\n\nThe CONTRACTOR shall perform the Services<!-- BRANCH:ENTITY --> using personnel and/or subcontractors of required skill, experience, and qualifications<!-- /BRANCH:ENTITY -->.\n\nThe CONTRACTOR shall perform the Services in a professional and workmanlike manner in accordance with best industry standards for similar services and shall devote adequate resources to meet its obligations under this Agreement.\n\nThe CONTRACTOR shall have full control and discretion over the means and methods for the performance of the Services and preparation of Deliverables, subject to strict compliance with this Agreement as well as any applicable legislations and regulations. The OH has no right or power to control or otherwise interfere with the CONTRACTOR's mode of performance under this Agreement.\n\nThe CONTRACTOR may render the Services from any place in the world except those under economic sanction by the United States federal government, the European Union, or the government of Switzerland. The CONTRACTOR has no desk or other equipment either located at or furnished by the OH.\n\n## 3. COLLABORATION\n\nThe Parties shall use their commercially reasonable efforts to collaborate in relation to the Services by responding promptly to any request, in a timely manner:\n\n* request by the CONTRACTOR to provide direction, information, approvals, authorizations, or decisions that are reasonably necessary to perform Services in accordance with the requirements of this Agreement, and\n* requests by the OH to obtain updates regarding the performance of Services, progress on Deliverables or any additional explanations which are reasonably necessary to assess or use the Deliverables.\n\n## 4. COMMENCEMENT AND TERM\n\n<!-- TERM:FIXED_DATE -->\nThe CONTRACTOR shall commence Services as a [Contractor Title] for the OH on [Work Start Date] and shall continue thereafter until [Work End Date].\n<!-- /TERM:FIXED_DATE -->\n<!-- TERM:ON_SOW_COMPLETION -->\nThe CONTRACTOR shall commence Services as a [Contractor Title] for the OH on [Work Start Date] and shall continue thereafter until the completion of the Services under all Statements of Work.\n<!-- /TERM:ON_SOW_COMPLETION -->\n<!-- TERM:NOTICE -->\nThe CONTRACTOR shall commence Services as a [Contractor Title] for the OH on [Work Start Date]. Either Party may terminate this Agreement or any Statement of Work with immediate effect, without cause, by providing at least [Termination Notice Period] calendar days’ prior written notice to the other Party.\n<!-- /TERM:NOTICE -->\n\nUpon expiration or termination of this Agreement for any reason, the CONTRACTOR shall promptly:\n\n* Deliver to the OH all documents, work product, and other materials, whether or not complete, prepared by or on behalf of the CONTRACTOR in the course of performing the Services;\n* Return to the OH all property, equipment, or materials owned by the OH, originating from the OH, or containing OH-Confidential Information that are in the CONTRACTOR’s possession or control. The CONTRACTOR shall also delete or securely destroy any copies of such property, equipment, or materials, ensuring that no unauthorized access or use is possible.\n\nClauses 9, 10, 11 and 12, along with any right or obligation of the Parties in this Agreement which, by its nature, should survive termination or expiration of this Agreement, will survive any such termination or expiration of this Agreement.\n\n## 5. REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES OF THE CONTRACTOR\n\nThe CONTRACTOR makes the following representations and warranties:\n\n* The CONTRACTOR complies with applicable law and regulation in its jurisdiction, including, but not limited to,\n  * having the legal capacity and clearance to execute, deliver and perform this Agreement including being of appropriate age,\n  * having the legitimate/appropriate business registration and working permits in the country where he is based and/or performing the Services,\n  * not operating their business while engaged with or within any entity under economic sanction by the governments of the United States, European Union, or Switzerland, and\n  * not being subject to any foreign exchange or regulatory restrictions applicable to receiving cryptographic assets,\n  * not being currently subject — to the CONTRACTOR’s knowledge — to any threatened claims, litigation or any legal or regulatory proceedings pending and that may impede performance under this Agreement;\n* The CONTRACTOR has the necessary skills and knowledge to perform and deliver the Services;\n* This Agreement is a valid and binding agreement and is fully enforceable against the CONTRACTOR;\n* The CONTRACTOR is not a party to or operating under any agreement, scheme, venture, understanding, obligation, duty, or similar that would prevent his entering into this Agreement or performing his obligations hereunder;\n* The CONTRACTOR satisfies all the conditions to be qualified as an independent contractor pursuant to the national law of whatever country in which this Agreement can be invoked in and, in particular, that the OH is not the sole entity procuring services from the CONTRACTOR at any given time;\n* Any Deliverables prepared or Service provided by the CONTRACTOR shall not infringe the intellectual property or other rights of any third party, and shall be free and clear of all encumbrances and liens of any kind;\n* The CONTRACTOR’s performance of this Agreement will not breach any confidentiality or other agreement with any former principal, employer or other third party, to which the CONTRACTOR is bound;\n* The CONTRACTOR shall not make any unauthorized use of confidential or proprietary information of any other person or entity;\n* The CONTRACTOR shall comply with applicable laws and regulations including registration with tax and other governmental authorities, filing of necessary tax forms and other reports, and the payment of proper taxes in the country where they may be owed by him.\n\n## 6. SERVICE FEE\n\nIn consideration of the provision of the Services and the rights granted to the OH under this Agreement, the OH shall pay the CONTRACTOR the fees set out in the applicable Statement of Work (“Service Fee”) and constituting payment in full for the performance of the Services outlined in the said Statement of Work, as well as of any Deliverables stemming therefrom.\n\nUnless otherwise provided in the applicable Statement of Work, the Service Fee will be payable within 30 days of receipt by the OH of an invoice from the CONTRACTOR. Except if otherwise agreed, the CONTRACTOR shall include in any invoice exclusively completed Services and Deliverables. Their satisfactory completion shall have been confirmed in writing by the OH. No payment shall be made if at the date of the invoice, the Services and/or Deliverables indicated therein are still pending.\n\nAll taxes, whether currently applicable or arising in the future, that are due to any taxation authority in connection with the Services shall be borne by the Party which is liable to pay the tax in accordance to applicable legislation.\n\nExcept as otherwise provided in the Statement of Work, all CONTRACTOR expenses shall be the sole responsibility of the CONTRACTOR unless approved in advance by the OH. In such case, the CONTRACTOR shall submit written documentation and official receipts on which relevant approved expenses are incurred in relation to his work. The OH shall pay the CONTRACTOR the expenses incurred based on the submission of documentations and receipts at the end of every month when the expenses were incurred.\n\nIn the event of termination of this Agreement, the OH’s sole obligation shall be to pay for Services already performed and Deliverables already accepted, pro-rata, and to reimburse authorized expenses incurred, prior to the termination date. The OH has no entitlement to fees already paid unless they were delivered for Services unrendered or illegally rendered.\n\n## 7. NO EMPLOYER-EMPLOYEE RELATIONSHIP\n\nThe CONTRACTOR is an independent contractor of the OH, and this Agreement shall not be construed to create any association, partnership, joint venture, employee, or agency relationship between the CONTRACTOR and the OH for any purpose. The CONTRACTOR has no authority (and shall not hold itself out as having authority) to bind the OH and the CONTRACTOR shall not make any agreements or representations on the OH’s behalf without the OH's prior written consent.\n\nWithout limiting the foregoing, the CONTRACTOR will not be eligible to participate in any vacation, group medical or life insurance, disability, profit sharing or retirement benefits, or any other fringe benefits or benefit plans offered by the OH to its employees, and the OH will not be responsible for withholding or paying any income, payroll or other federal, state, or local taxes, making any insurance contributions such as social security, pension fund and professional welfare insurance, or any other insurance (including professional and private accidents' insurances, etc.). The CONTRACTOR shall be responsible for, and shall indemnify the OH against, all such taxes or contributions, including penalties and interest.\n\n<!-- BRANCH:ENTITY -->\nAny persons employed or engaged by the CONTRACTOR in connection with the performance of the Services shall be the CONTRACTOR's employees or contractors and the CONTRACTOR shall be fully responsible for them and indemnify the OH against any claims made by or on behalf of any such employee or contractor.\n<!-- /BRANCH:ENTITY -->\n\n## 8. IP ASSIGNMENT\n\n### (a) Definitions\n\nFor the purposes of this Agreement:\n\n“Developed IP” means any Intellectual Property Rights which are developed, prepared, conceived, made or suggested by the CONTRACTOR or by any employee or contractor of CONTRACTOR as part of, in connection with, arising out of or in relationship to the performance of Services under this Agreement.\n\n“Intellectual Property Rights” shall mean any intellectual property rights or other proprietary rights throughout the world, in any media, whether currently existing or created in the future, applicable to all versions, elements, and languages, and for the entire duration of such rights, to the maximum extent permitted by law. These rights may arise under statutory law, civil or common law, contract, or otherwise, and include both registered and unregistered rights, as well as those that are registrable or not, including without limitation:\n\n* rights associated with works of authorship, including copyrights, related database rights, applications for copyright registration, and registered copyrights;\n* rights in computer software, source code, object code, algorithms, or business methods;\n* rights in trademarks, service marks, trade names, business names, internet domain names, logos, trade dress, including applications for registration and registrations thereof;\n* rights in inventions, discoveries, utility models, patents, reissues, re-examinations, as well as patent applications (wherever filed, registered, issued or not, including continuations, continuations-in-part, substitutes, divisions, and priority rights stemming from such applications), whether existing now or filed, issued, or acquired in the future;\n* rights related to the protection of trade secrets, know-how, and other confidential information;\n* design rights, whether registered or unregistered;\n* rights in materials, including but not limited to documents, manuals, and content, regardless of the format;\n* any rights analogous to those listed above, and any and all other proprietary rights relating to intangible property, including rights that may not fall squarely into one of the categories above but are nonetheless legally protected.\n\n### (b) Assignment\n\n* Notwithstanding anything to the contrary in this Agreement, the CONTRACTOR shall assign and hereby assigns to the OH all Intellectual Property Rights in Developed IP, including all modifications, improvements, and derivative works thereof, whether solely or jointly created. Such assignment shall be effective upon creation and shall include all present and future rights to Developed IP. The CONTRACTOR will do all things and execute all documents necessary to secure the OH’s ownership of the Intellectual Property Rights in Developed IP.\n* Except for any confidential or proprietary materials in which the CONTRACTOR has a pre-existing Intellectual Property Rights (\"Existing Materials\") and subject at all times to section 8(b)(i) above, any and all analyses, evaluations, reports, memoranda, letters, processes, methods, programs, and manuals and any improvements, enhancements, or modifications to any of the foregoing shall be and remain the exclusive property of the OH.\n* To the extent that Developed IP may incorporate or require the use of Existing Materials, the CONTRACTOR shall notify OH of such intent prior to commencement of the performance of Services. To the extent that Existing Materials are incorporated into the Developed IP, the CONTRACTOR grants the OH, its successors, assignees, licensees and any third party authorized by the OH a royalty-free, irrevocable, worldwide, sublicensable, transferrable, non-exclusive, perpetual right to use, modify, and prepare derivative works of such Existing Materials, and to use and display such Existing Materials, with full rights to authorize others to do the same but only to the extent required to utilize the Developed IP in accordance with the ownership rights granted in this Agreement.\n* The CONTRACTOR represents and warrants that, to the best of their knowledge, the Developed IP will not infringe upon any third-party Intellectual Property Rights. Where third-party Intellectual Property Rights are used in the performance of the services (“Third-Party IP”), the CONTRACTOR shall notify it and ensure that they have obtained all necessary licenses and permissions to use such Third-Party IP, and that such licenses are sufficient to grant the OH, its successors, assignees, licensees and any third party authorized by the OH the right to use, modify, and distribute the Third-Party IP to the maximum extent necessary to fulfil the purposes of this Agreement.\n\n### (c) Moral Rights\n\nTo the extent that moral rights of the CONTRACTOR in Developed IP are assignable to the OH, the CONTRACTOR hereby assigns such rights to the OH. To the extent such rights are not assignable, the CONTRACTOR agrees to waive such moral rights in the Existing Materials and Developed IP to the maximum extent permitted by law. To the extent such rights can neither be waived nor assigned, the CONTRACTOR grants consent to (and will obtain all other necessary written consents to) the OH, its successors, assignees, licensees and any third party authorized by the OH in carrying out any activity, including any acts or omissions to act, the performance or non-performance of which would otherwise infringe the CONTRACTOR's moral rights in Existing Materials and Developed IP.\n\n## 9. NON-DISCLOSURE AND CONFIDENTIALITY\n\nAll non-public, confidential or proprietary information of each Party (\"Confidential Information\"), including, but not limited to, specifications, samples, patterns, designs, plans, drawings, documents, data or operations disclosed by one Party to the other Party, whether disclosed orally or disclosed or accessed in written, electronic, or other form or media, and whether or not marked, designated, or otherwise identified as \"confidential\", in connection with this Agreement is confidential, solely for use in connection with this Agreement and may not be disclosed or copied unless authorized by the disclosing Party in writing.\n\nConfidential Information does not include any information that: (i) is or becomes generally available to the public other than as a result of the receiving Party's breach of this Agreement; (ii) is obtained by the receiving Party on a non-confidential basis from a third-party that was not legally or contractually restricted from disclosing such information; (iii) the receiving Party establishes by documentary evidence, was in the receiving Party's possession prior to the disclosing Party's disclosure hereunder; or (iv) was or is independently developed by the receiving Party without using any Confidential Information from the disclosing Party.\n\nSpecifically, except as authorized by the other Party or as it may be required by binding law or court order, the Parties shall not at any time or in any manner, either directly or indirectly, divulge, disclose, or communicate to any third-party in any manner whatsoever any Confidential Information concerning\n\n* Their relationship under this Agreement;\n* The Services and Deliverables provided under this Agreement; and\n* Their respective third-party relations, including but not limited to those with other service-providers, investors, contributors, and client entities.\n\nUpon termination of this Agreement, the CONTRACTOR shall deliver upon request to a representative of the OH or destroy upon request by the OH all proprietary or Confidential Information in documentary or tangible form, including copies or reproductions then in his possession or under his control from the OH; provided, however, that the CONTRACTOR may retain a copy of such Confidential Information for the purposes of complying with any legal obligations and subject to any copies remaining on the CONTRACTOR’s standard computer back-up devices (which copies the CONTRACTOR agrees not to access after termination).\n\n## 10. CYBERSECURITY\n\nWhile performing the Services described in this Agreement, the CONTRACTOR shall implement and maintain cyber security measures, including data security measures, that are consistent with the standards and best practices applicable to their professional designation under this Agreement.\n\nThe OH reserves the right to define, within the Statement of Work, any industry standards, or specific requirements that the CONTRACTOR must comply with in relation to a particular Service, Deliverable, or more generally under this Agreement. Furthermore, the OH may also specify in the Statement of Work that the CONTRACTOR is required to comply with particular regulations and laws governing data security and protection that are applicable to the Services or Deliverables being provided. The CONTRACTOR shall ensure full adherence to such specified standards, requirements, regulations, and laws as outlined by the OH.\n\nUpon termination of this Agreement and unless otherwise authorized by the OH in writing, the CONTRACTOR shall relinquish access to any development environments, subscription services, storage drives, repositories, accounts, digital ledgers, or web applications belonging to the OH, its successors, assignees, agents, or as otherwise gained through the course of work performed under this Agreement. The CONTRACTOR shall further cease storage of any data belonging to the OH, its successors, assignees, agents, or as otherwise gained through the course of work performed under this Agreement.\n\n## 11. LIMITATIONS OF LIABILITY\n\nTo the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, neither Party, nor any of their respective past, present, or future board members, founders, employees, officers, directors, contractors, consultants, suppliers, vendors, service providers, developers, subsidiaries, affiliates, agents, representatives, predecessors, successors, or assignees, shall be liable for any direct damages of any kind.\n\nThis includes, but is not limited to, loss of revenue, income, or profits; loss of data or its use; business interruption; or diminution in value, arising out of or in any way related to this Agreement, regardless of the form of action—whether in contract, tort (including but not limited to simple negligence, whether active, passive, or imputed), or any other legal theory. This limitation applies even if the Party has been advised of the possibility of such damages or if such damages were otherwise foreseeable.\n\nHowever, this exclusion does not limit or exclude liability for gross negligence, fraud, or willful misconduct by either Party.\n\n## 12. FORCE MAJEURE\n\nNeither party shall be liable for any delay or failure in performance under this Agreement resulting directly or indirectly from acts of god, civil or military authority, war, fire, explosions, earthquakes, floods, or any other cause beyond the control of either Party, provided no fault or negligence on the part of a Party was involved.\n\n## 13. FORM\n\nAny reference to \"writing\" or \"written\" includes any legible reproduction of words delivered in permanent and tangible form (includes electronic signature, such as DocuSign or AdobeSign, or scan of the signature on a scanned document or an electronic file).\n\n## 14. ASSIGNMENT\n\nNeither Party may assign any of its rights or obligations under this Agreement without the other Party’s prior written consent. Otherwise, any assignment done contrary to this provision shall be without effect and shall be ground for the immediate termination of this Agreement without need of notice.\n\n## 15. GOVERNING LAW, JURISDICTION, AND ARBITRATION\n\nThis Agreement will be governed by and construed according to the laws of Switzerland, excluding Swiss conflicts of law rules. The United Nations Convention on the International Sale of Goods shall not apply.\n\nEach Party submits to the jurisdiction of the courts of the Canton of [Canton], Switzerland.\n\nAny dispute arising out of or in connection with this Agreement shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the Courts of the canton of [Canton], Switzerland (exclusive venue).\n\n## 16. SEVERABILITY\n\nIf any provision of this Agreement shall be found to be invalid or inoperative under Swiss law, such provision shall be construed to make it enforceable to the greatest extent permitted, shall remain in effect to the greatest extent permitted, and all other provisions shall remain in full force and effect.\n\n## 17. WAIVER\n\nNo waiver by the OH of any breach of this Agreement shall be a waiver of any preceding or succeeding breach. No waiver by the OH of any right under this Agreement shall be construed as a waiver of any other right.\n\nNo waiver by the CONTRACTOR of any breach of this Agreement shall be a waiver of any preceding or succeeding breach. No waiver by the CONTRACTOR of any right under this Agreement shall be construed as a waiver of any other right.\n\nIN WITNESS WHEREOF, the Parties hereto have set their hands on the date written below.\n\n| | |\n| --- | --- |\n| [Association Name] | <!-- BRANCH:ENTITY -->[Contractor Entity Name]<!-- /BRANCH:ENTITY --><!-- BRANCH:INDIVIDUAL -->[Contractor Name]<!-- /BRANCH:INDIVIDUAL --> |\n| Operational Hub, represented by [OH Agent] | Contractor<!-- BRANCH:ENTITY -->, represented by [Contractor Name]<!-- /BRANCH:ENTITY --> |\n| Date: | Date: |\n\n---\n\n## List of Schedules\n\n* Schedule A – Statement of Work\n* Schedule B – Compensation Structure\n\n[REMAINDER OF PAGE INTENTIONALLY LEFT BLANK]\n\n---\n\n## Schedule A: Statement of Work [SOW Number]\n\nDate: [Contract Date]\n\nTHIS STATEMENT OF WORK is entered as of the Effective Date designated below, by and between CONTRACTOR (as defined below) and the OH (as defined below); CONTRACTOR and the OH together referred to as (\"Parties\"), each of them a (\"Party\").\n\nThe Parties hereto acknowledge that they are entering into this Statement of Work pursuant to the provisions of the Contractor Agreement dated as of [Contract Date] by and between [Contractor Name] of [Contractor Address] (\"CONTRACTOR\") and [Association Name], [Registered Address], Switzerland (“OH”; the \"Agreement\"). The Parties further acknowledge and agree that the provisions of the Contractor Agreement are hereby incorporated by reference and shall apply to this Statement of Work as though set forth herein in their entirety. All capitalized terms not otherwise defined herein shall have the meaning set forth in the Agreement.\n\nThe terms and conditions set forth in this Statement of Work shall apply only to the Services covered by this Statement of Work and not to Services covered under any other Statement of Work and shall not amend or supplement the terms of the Agreement except for purposes of the Services covered by this Statement of Work.\n\n### 1. Scope of Services and Deliverables\n\nCONTRACTOR will provide the following services and deliverables to the OH (the \"Services\" and the \"Deliverables\"):\n\n* [Services To Be Rendered]\n\nThe OH may further define the Services above through requests outlining specific work products and materials (each, a “Request”) to be delivered to the OH as part of the performance of the Services (each, a \"Deliverable\"). Requests can be submitted in writing or per email or any messaging application used for communications with the OH while performing Services.\n\nThe OH may include in the Request detailed specifications, a delivery timeline, and an approval process for the Deliverable.\n\n### 2. Scope of Commitment\n\nThe CONTRACTOR agrees to provide professional services for a total of [FTE Hours] worked hours delivered per year.\n\n2.1 Time commitment represents the CONTRACTOR's agreed-upon level of engagement and availability for project work, meetings, and deliverables.\n\n2.2 The CONTRACTOR shall allocate time and resources consistent with this designation, ensuring substantive and consistent contribution to project objectives.\n\n2.3 This time commitment may be adjusted by mutual written agreement between the parties, with any modifications documented as a formal amendment to this agreement.\n\n### 3. Performance Expectations\n\nThe CONTRACTOR agrees to allocate sufficient time and expertise to provide the Services in good faith and to coordinate with OH stakeholders as needed to ensure effective delivery. The CONTRACTOR understands that the designation implies a substantial and meaningful work commitment and does not preclude additional project-specific arrangements. This Agreement does not require exclusive availability or fixed working hours.\n\n[REMAINDER OF PAGE INTENTIONALLY LEFT BLANK]\n\n---\n\n## Schedule B: Compensation Structure\n\nMonthly Fee: [Compensation Amount] excl. VAT (if any).\n\nCash paid per month: in [Denomination Type]\n\n### Payment Specifications\n\nCurrency specification: Paid in [Denomination Currency]\n\nPayment is processed in the third week of the following month.\n\nPayment in [Denomination Currency] to be made to a bank account specified by the contractor.\n\nPayment in crypto to be made to an address specified by the contractor.\n\n[REMAINDER OF PAGE INTENTIONALLY LEFT BLANK]\n";

export const mpaV2TemplateRaw = "**MULTISIGNATURE PARTICIPATION AGREEMENT**\n\n**(“Agreement”)**\n\nbetween\n\n\\[Association Name\\], an association incorporated in Zug, Switzerland \n\n(“**Association**”)\n\nAnd\n\n\\[Active Signer  Personal Name\\], \\[Citizenship\\], residing in \\[Residence Country\\] \n\n/\n\n\\[Active Signer Entity Name\\], incorporated in (Incorporation City, Incorporation Country\\]\n\n(“**Active Signer**”)\n\n(Each a “**Party**”, collectively the “**Parties**”)\n\n**PREAMBLE**\n\n**WHEREAS** the purpose of the Association is to orchestrate collaboration and provide operational support for teams building technological public goods.\n\n**WHEREAS** the Association holds, among other assets, an operational budget dedicated for the development of specific public goods which it manages in line with its purpose (\"**Designated Ops Budget**\"). \n\n**WHEREAS** the Association keeps the Designated Ops Budget in self-custody in the wallets listed under Exhibit 1 (“**Wallet**”). \n\n**WHEREAS** to ensure the secure storage and management of the Designated Ops Budget, the Association wishes to implement a multisignature scheme, requiring Wallet transactions to be approved by multiple members acting as designated signatories within the governance of the Association (“**Multisignature Scheme**”). \n\n**WHEREAS** the Active Signer is a member of the Association (“**Membe**r”) and is willing to act as a signer in the Multisignature Scheme. \n\n**WHEREAS** the Parties recognize the importance of ensuring that the Multisignature Scheme is managed securely, transparently, and effectively. This Agreement establishes the framework, responsibilities, and processes to govern the coordination and operation of the Wallet(s), ensuring compliance with the Association's purpose and applicable laws.\n\n**NOW, THEREFORE,** in consideration of the Preamble, the mutual covenants contained in this Agreement, and other good and valuable consideration, the receipt and sufficiency of which are hereby acknowledged, the Parties agree as follows:\n\n1. **ASSOCIATION WALLET** \n\nThe Designated Ops Budget is held in the Wallet governed by the Multisignature Scheme outlined in Exhibit 2. \n\nIf the event that multiple addresses are associated with the Wallet, Exhibit 2 shall detail any deviations to the Multisignature Scheme where such deviations apply to a specific Wallet. \n\nThe Wallet shall be used exclusively for Designated Ops Budget funds and shall not store any unrelated assets.  The Active Signer shall not accept any funds into the Wallet for their own account or the account of third parties.\n\nThe Wallet and the related assets held in the Wallet are the property of the Association and remains under its exclusive control. The Active Signer holds no rights, title, or personal interest in any assets stored therein by virtue of this Agreement.\n\nBy joining the Multisignature Scheme, the Active Signer neither receives nor holds funds on behalf of the Association and does not act in a fiduciary capacity.\n\nThe Association may create additional Wallets to the Multisignature Scheme. In this case, the Parties shall amend Exhibit 1 accordingly. \n\n2. **ACTIVE SIGNER ROLE** \n\nBy executing this Agreement, the Active Signer:\n\n(i)\tAccepts their role as a participant to the Multisignature Scheme;  \n(ii)\tAccepts to be entrusted with a Key; and  \n(iii)\tAgrees to receive and process Signature Requests.\n\nThrough participation in the Multisignature Scheme, the Active Signer does not gain any additional decision-making authority beyond their role as a Member. Instead, the Active Signer serves a purely technical function within the Association, without control or disposal rights over the Designated Ops Budget or Wallet(s). \n\nThe role of the Active Signer is limited to executing transactions in line with the process outline in Exhibit 2, on behalf of and in the name of the Association, and strictly in accordance with validly adopted decisions approved by the Members and  Accordingly, the Active Signer is responsible for the orderly administration of the Wallet and the proper deployment of the Designated Ops Budget in alignment with the Association’s decisions.\n\nThe role of Active Signer is strictly personal and cannot be delegated, assigned, or otherwise transferred to any third party. The Active Signer shall not execute this Agreement on behalf of any third party. Furthermore, the Key must not be shared, disclosed, or made accessible to anyone other than the designated Active Signer.\n\nThe role as an Active Signer is performed as a Member of the Association. The Active Signer receives no compensation and is not entitled to reimbursement of expenses.\n\n3. **MULTISIGNATURE SCHEME** \n\nAny Active Signer may initiate a message disseminated to the remaining participants in the Multisignature Scheme and requesting them to sign a transaction with their Key (“**Signature Request**”). \n\nThe Association ensures that the Multisignature Scheme is set up in a manner which allows transactions to be executed without the participation of the Active Signer necessarily responding to each Signature Request. \n\nSignature Requests shall be initiated and responded to in accordance with this Section, the details provided under Exhibit 2 as well as any other procedures and guidelines set forth by the Association, as listed under Exhibit 3 (“**Internal Policies**”). \n\nActive Signers shall not intentionally refrain from responding to a Signature Request, unless there are valid grounds to contest it. In such cases, they must promptly communicate these grounds to all other Active Signers.\n\n4. **OBLIGATIONS OF THE ACTIVE SIGNERS**\n\n   1. **General** \n\nActive Signers shall perform their duties with due diligence, care, and professionalism, and shall act honestly, ethically, and in good faith, free from personal bias or conflict of interest, in all aspects of their role.\n\n2. **Critical Review and Reporting**\n\nActive Signers must critically review each Signature Request before approving it, ensuring that it aligns with the decisions of the Association and the decision itself aligns with the defined governance process.\n\nIf any concerns arise about a proposed transaction, Active Signers are obligated to immediately report it to other Active Signers and provide all relevant information regarding their concerns.\n\n3. **Collaboration** \n\nActive Signers must maintain open lines of communication with each other, ensuring transparency. This includes sharing relevant information regarding the status of a Signature Request or any issues encountered.\n\nBeyond the consultation or collaboration expressly required under this Agreement, the Parties are expected to engage in proactive, prompt, frequent, and timely consultation and cooperation on all matters related to the Multisignature Scheme and the Wallet, ensuring that all decisions, transactions, and actions taken are well-informed and aligned with the best interests of the Association.\n\n4. **Security of the Key**\n\nThe Active Signer is solely responsible for the secure storage and protection of their assigned Key. The Key must be stored in a secure manner that prevents unauthorized access, loss, theft, or compromise. The Active Signer must take all necessary precautions to protect the security of the Key and by extension, of the Wallet. The Active Signer acknowledges the security guidelines in Exhibit 2 and shall strictly comply therewith, as these may be amended by the Association at any time.\n\nThe Active Signer shall participate in any security procedures mandated by the Association to ensure the security of the Wallet and the Multisignature Scheme, such as participation in regular testing. \n\nIn the event of a suspected or actual compromise, loss, or theft of a Key, or any detected suspicious or irregular activity related to the Multisignature Scheme, Wallet, transactions, or decision-making process, the Active Signer shall immediately notify the Association and all other Active Signers in writing. The notification must detail the incident and any risk mitigation measures taken. If necessary, the notification shall also be forwarded to the appropriate authorities.\n\nAny effective loss or unauthorized access or compromise of a Key results in the automatic de-permission of the concerned Key and termination of this Agreement with the concerned Active Signer, to be replaced by a new one within seven (7) calendar days.\n\n5. **Availability** \n\nIn cases of inability to perform their duties, Active Signers must notify the other Active Signers immediately, when possible, and ensure that a clear plan is in place to guarantee that their duties can be fulfilled without interruption.\n\nActive Signers must avoid being unavailable, i.e., without network access or means of communication, for more than \\[X days/hours\\] without prior notification, unless such unavailability results from unforeseeable circumstances, such as force majeure or illness. \n\n5. **CONFIDENTIALITY**\n\nActive Signers shall not disclose their role, the existence of the Multisignature Scheme nor its details to any third Parties. Active Signers shall besides maintain the confidentiality of all sensitive information related to the transactions, decisions, and financial matters of the Association. \n\nDisclosure of such information should only be made when required by law or in the course of their duties.\n\nThe Active Signer has the right to remain anonymous towards third parties and not disclosed as a participant of the Multisignature Scheme. \n\nIn such cases, discussions and communications involving the Active Signer referring to the identity or elements allowing the identification of the Active Signer shall be conspicuously marked as \"confidential\" and shall be deemed \"Confidential Information\". \n\nThe Association shall maintain the confidentiality of, and shall not disclose, publish or make available, all Confidential Information: provided, however, that the foregoing covenants shall not apply to particular Confidential Information to the extent that: (a) such Confidential Information becomes widely known to the public (other than through a breach of this Agreement); (b) such Confidential Information is required to be disclosed pursuant to the applicable laws or regulations or orders of the court or other government authorities applicable to the Association (provided that the Association provides the Active Signer with written notice sufficiently in advance of such disclosure to afford such Parties the other opportunity to seek a protective order or otherwise limit the disclosure of such Confidential Information); or (c) such Confidential Information is disclosed by the Association to its legal counsels or financial advisors with a need to know such Confidential Information in order to provide advice regarding the transactions contemplated hereunder, provided that such legal counsels or financial advisors, as the case may be, are apprised of the confidential nature of such Confidential Information and are bound by the confidentiality obligations to the Association with respect thereto similar to those set forth in this section. \n\nThis section shall survive the termination of this Agreement for any reason. \n\nNotwithstanding the above, any Active Signer may, for themselves only (and assuming all risks that may arise from such disclosure), make public their status as an Active Signer, but not the existence, terms, or conditions of this Agreement. \n\n6. **REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES OF THE ACTIVE SIGNERS**\n\n   1. **Capacity and authority**\n\nThe Active Signer represents and warrants having all requisite capacity, power and authority to enter into, and to perform, hold, assume, undertake, and exercise all rights, powers, duties, obligations, and liabilities applicable to the Active Signer thereunder, and the foregoing constitute the legal, valid and binding obligation of the Active Signer, enforceable against the Active Signer in accordance with their terms, except as limited by applicable bankruptcy, insolvency, reorganization, moratorium, fraudulent conveyance, and any other laws of general application affecting enforcement of creditors’ rights generally, and as limited by laws relating to the availability of specific performance, injunctive relief, or other equitable remedies.\n\n2. **Non-Contravention**\n\nThis Agreement and the Active Signer’s rights, powers, duties, obligations, and liabilities thereunder do not contravene, conflict with, or violate or constitute a breach or default under (or an event that with notice or lapse of time or both would become a violation or constitute a breach or default under) any applicable legal requirement, or agreement to which the Signer is subject or a party or by which the Active Signer or any asset of the Active Signer is bound.\n\n3. **Compliance**\n\nThe Active Signer undertakes to promptly provide, or cause to be provided to the Association, or to a service provider chosen by the Association, all required information, including supporting documentation and other evidence, as may be reasonably requested by the Association, to fully identify the Active Signer and if required, ensure compliance with applicable anti-money laundering legislations. All information provided by the Active Signer in such context shall true, accurate and up to date. \n\nThe Active Signer along with its affiliates, officers, and directors, is not a resident, citizen, or located in a geographic area subject to sanctions or embargoes imposed by the United Nations, or listed in the Swiss SECO’s Overall List of Sanctioned Individuals, Entities and Organizations, the EU Consolidated List of Persons, Groups, and Entities Subject to EU Financial Sanctions, US Department of Commerce’s Denied Persons or Entity List, the US Department of Treasury’s Specially Designated Nationals or Blocked Persons Lists, the US Department of State’s Debarred Parties List, or subject to any other national or pan-national sanctions or embargoes. Furthermore, they are not listed on, nor associated with, any person or entity subject to such sanctions or embargoes\n\n4. **No Required Consents**\n\nThe Active Signer will not be required to make any filing with or give any notice to, or to obtain any approval, clearance, consent, ratification, permission, waiver, or authorization (including any governmental authorization) from, any person in connection with the execution, delivery, or performance of this Agreement.\n\n5. **Experience and Knowledge**\n\nThe Active Signer is a sophisticated, experienced, and knowledgeable professional in blockchain technologies, crypto assets, and multisignature schemes. They fully understand the associated risks and are well-versed in the best practices and preventive measures required to mitigate them.\n\n6. **No Convictions**\n\nThe Active Signer has not been convicted of or held liable for fraud, wilful misconduct, gross negligence, breach of fiduciary duty, or (in connection with the Active Signer’s professional or commercial activities) a crime of moral turpitude.\n\n7. **LIABILITY OF ACTIVE SIGNERS**\n\nTo the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, the Active Signer shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or exemplary damages, including but not limited to damages for loss of profits, revenues, customers, opportunities, goodwill, use, or data, even if the Active Signer has been advised of the possibility of such damages.\n\nTo the extent permitted under applicable law, each Party, on its own behalf and on behalf of its successors, heirs, and assigns, hereby fully and forever releases and discharges each other Party, along with its respective agents, nominees, attorneys, insurers, successors, heirs, and assigns, from any and all claims, counterclaims, defences, setoffs, recoupments, debts, demands, causes of action, suits, obligations, injuries, losses, damages, costs, expenses, attorneys' and expert witness fees, and liabilities of any kind, whether in law or equity, arising under statute, contract, or tort, whether known or unknown, fixed or contingent, related to the Key and participation in the Multisignature Scheme, and any other claims that could be raised in connection therewith, \n\nEach Party assumes the risk of any factual error, whether mutual or unilateral, concerning any claims. Under no circumstances shall any Party seek to present claims against another Party arising from any actions or inactions related to participation in the Multisignature Scheme.\n\n8. **TERMINATION** \n\n   This Agreement shall commence as of the date set out on the Effective Date and shall continue thereafter for an indefinite period (“**Term**”). \n\n   Both Parties have the right to terminate this Agreement at any time, with or without cause, with immediate effect.\n\nThe Agreement is automatically terminated in the event of a material breach of this Agreement, such as:\n\n* Failure to disclose conflicts of interest unless affirmatively disclosed and, if applicable, consented to in accordance with Section 9**.**  \n* Repeated failure to respond in a timely to Signature Requests.  \n* Breach of confidentiality obligations set forth in Section 5**.**  \n* Any other material failure to comply with this Agreement.\n\nThe material breach and ensuing termination shall be documented and recorded in a decision of the Association.\n\nIn the event of a material breach of this Agreement by an Active Signer, and to the extent permitted by applicable law, termination of this Agreement shall be the sole remedy available to the Parties for breach or non-performance of this Agreement. Accordingly, the Association agrees that, as a material inducement to engage participants to hold Keys, it shall not pursue other legal remedies against the Active Signer and waives any contractual legal claims.\n\nUpon termination of this Agreement, the Active Signer shall immediately: \n\n* be de-permissioned and thereby prevented from further using the Key.  \n* no longer receive or be informed of Signature Requests.  \n* fully relinquish or destroy the Key.   \n* lose all rights, powers, and privileges under this Agreement, including any related to the Wallet.\n\n  The Active Signer’s duties relevant to the security and safekeeping of the Key under this Agreement shall continue until the Active Signer has effectively relinquished or destroyed such Key(s). \n\nAll obligations and liabilities of the Active Signer under the provisions of this Agreement that by their nature are intended or customarily do survive a termination of contract (including confidentiality obligations) shall survive and be continuing\n\n9. **CONFLICTS OF INTEREST**\n\nThe Active Signer shall continuously monitor and evaluate their own personal facts and circumstances (including a direct and indirect business and other economic interests in the Designated Ops Budget) that could reasonably be expected to give rise to a material conflict of interest in connection with the Active Signer’s performance of their role and duties under this Agreement. \n\nThe Active Signer may, from time to time, contribute, whether voluntarily or for remuneration, to public goods funded through the Designated Ops Budget. However, such contributions shall be subject to the conflict of interest provisions outlined in this section.\n\n1. **Ongoing Conflicts of Interest**\n\nIf the Active Signer becomes aware of an ongoing material conflict of interest with respect to the execution of their respective role hereunder, the Active Signer shall promptly resign or otherwise be removed from participation in their role in accordance with the provisions contained herein, unless such conflict of interest has been disclosed to the Association and other participants to the Multisignature Scheme in reasonable detail, and a majority of the Association consented to retaining their role as Active Signer notwithstanding such conflict of interest (which consent, for the avoidance of doubt, may be conditioned on appropriate disclosure to defined parties). \n\n2.  **One-Off Conflicts of Interest.** \n\nIf the Active Signer becomes aware of a material conflict of interest with respect to any specific Signature Request, the Active Signer shall promptly disclose such conflict of interest to the Association and other participants to the Multisignature Scheme and refrain from further involvement with such Signature Request. \n\n10. **MISCELLANEOUS** \n\n    1. **Entire Agreement**\n\nThis Agreement, its Exhibits and any document incorporated thereto by reference, constitute the full and entire understanding and agreement between the Parties with respect to the subject matter hereof, and any other written or oral agreement relating to the subject matter hereof existing between the Parties are expressly voided.\n\n2.     **Amendment**\n\nNo amendment to or modification of or rescission, termination or discharge of this Agreement, including any schedule, is effective unless it is in writing, identified as an amendment to or rescission, termination or discharge of this Agreement and signed by an authorized representative of each Party.\n\n3.   **Successors and Assigns.** \n\nThis Agreement is personal to each of the Parties hereto. No Party may assign voluntarily or by operation of law or delegate any rights or obligations hereunder without first obtaining the written consent of all the other Parties hereto. Any attempted assignment or transfer by any Party without such consent shall be void ab initio. \n\nThe terms and conditions of this Agreement shall inure to the benefit of and be binding upon the respective successors and permitted assigns of the Parties. Nothing in this Agreement, express or implied, is intended to confer upon any Party other than the Parties hereto or their respective successors and assigns any rights, remedies, obligations or liabilities under or by reason of this Agreement, except as expressly provided in this Agreement. \n\n4.      **Counterparts.** \n\nThis Agreement may be executed in any number of separate counterparts, each of which when executed and delivered shall be an original, but all of which together shall constitute one and the same instrument. Counterparts may be delivered via facsimile, electronic mail (including pdf or any electronic signature complying with the U.S. federal ESIGN Act of 2000, e.g., www.docusign.com) or other transmission method and any counterpart so delivered shall be deemed to have been duly and validly delivered and be valid and effective for all purposes. \n\n5.      **Severability**     \n\nAny term or provision of this Agreement that is found invalid or unenforceable in any situation in any jurisdiction shall not affect the validity or enforceability of the remaining terms and provisions hereof or the validity or enforceability of the offending term or provision in any other situation or in any other jurisdiction. If a final judgment of a court of competent jurisdiction declares that any term or provision hereof is invalid or unenforceable, the Parties hereto agree that the court making such determination shall have the power to limit such term or provision, to delete specific words or phrases, or to replace any invalid or unenforceable term or provision with a term or provision that is valid and enforceable and that comes closest to expressing the intention of the invalid or unenforceable term or provision, and this Agreement shall be enforceable as so modified. In the event such court does not exercise the power granted to it in the prior sentence, the Parties hereto agree to replace such invalid or unenforceable term or provision with a valid and enforceable term or provision that will achieve, to the extent possible, the economic, business and other purposes of such invalid or unenforceable term or provision. \n\n6.  **Waiver; Delays or Omissions.** \n\nNo delay or omission to exercise any right, power or remedy accruing to any Party under this Agreement, upon any breach or default of any other Party under this Agreement, shall impair any such right, power or remedy of such non-breaching or non-defaulting Party nor shall it be construed to be a waiver of any such breach or default, or an acquiescence therein, or of or in any similar breach or default thereafter occurring; nor shall any waiver of any single breach or default be deemed a waiver of any other breach or default theretofore or thereafter occurring. Any waiver, permit, consent or approval of any kind or character on the part of any Party of any breach or default under this Agreement, or any waiver on the part of any Party of any provisions or conditions of this Agreement, must be in writing and shall be effective only to the extent specifically set forth in such writing. \n\n7.      **Parties in Interest.** \n\nAll third-party rights are expressly disclaimed. This Agreement is intended for the benefit of the Parties hereto and their respective permitted successors and assigns, and is not for the benefit of, nor any provision hereof be enforced by, any other party. None of the provisions of this Agreement are intended to provide any rights or remedies to any employee, creditor, Contributor, or other person other than the Parties and their respective heirs, successors and assigns (if any). \n\n8.      **Further Assurances.** \n\nEach Party shall execute and cause to be delivered to the other Parties such instruments and other documents, and shall take such other actions, as any other Party may reasonably request for the purpose of carrying out or evidencing any of the matters contemplated by this Agreement. \n\n9. **Rules of Construction.** \n\nFor purposes of this Agreement, whenever the context requires: the singular number shall include the plural, and vice versa; the masculine gender shall include the feminine and neuter genders; the feminine gender shall include the masculine and neuter genders; and the neuter gender shall include the masculine and feminine genders. \n\nThe Parties hereto agree that any rule of construction to the effect that ambiguities are to be resolved against the drafting Party shall not be applied in the construction or interpretation of this Agreement. \n\nAs used in this Agreement, the words \"include,\" \"including,\" \"such as\" and variations thereof, shall not be deemed to be terms of limitation, but rather shall be deemed to be followed by the words \"without limitation.\" The word \"or\" shall mean the non-exclusive \"or\". \n\nExcept as otherwise indicated, all references in this Agreement to \"Sections,\" \"Schedules\" and \"Exhibits\" are intended to refer to Sections of this Agreement and Schedules and Exhibits to this Agreement. \n\nThe terms \"hereof,\" \"herein,\" \"hereunder,\" \"hereby\" and \"herewith\" and words of similar import will, unless otherwise stated, be construed to refer to this Agreement as a whole and not to any particular provision of this Agreement. \n\n11. **APPLICABLE LAW AND JURISDICTION**\n\nThis Agreement and all claims relating to or arising out of this Agreement, or the breach thereof, whether in contract, tort or otherwise, shall be governed by Swiss law, excluding Swiss choice of law principles and excluding international treaties. \n\nAny dispute, controversy or claim arising out of or in connection to this Agreement, including the validity, invalidity, breach, or termination thereof, shall be exclusively resolved by the ordinary courts of Zug, Switzerland.\n\n**LIST OF EXHIBITS**\n\n**Exhibit 1** – Wallet Description\n\n**Exhibit 2** – Multisignature Scheme Description and Process\n\n**Exhibit 3** – List of Internal Policies \n\n\\[SIGNATURE PAGES FOLLOWS\\]\n\n \n\n| The Association   |  |   |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| \\[*Name, function*\\] |  | *Place, date* |\n|   |  |   |\n| \\[*Name, function*\\] |  | *Place, date* |\n\n**The Active Signer**\n\n|   |  |   |\n| :---- | :---- | :---- |\n| \\[*Name*\\] |  | *Place, date* |\n\n2. \n\n   \n\n   **EXHIBIT 1 – WALLET DESCRIPTION**\n\n   1. **Description**\n\nThe Multisignature Scheme includes Number of Keys Keys, one of which is held by the Active Signer. \\[Decision Quorum\\] signatures out of the Number of Keys Keys (“**Decision Quorum**”) are required to execute a transaction with the Wallet. The Decision Quorum can be amended by decision of the Association. \n\nThe Multisignature Scheme relies on the following signature platform (“\\[**Multisignature Platform\\]**”):\n\n| \\[Wallet Address\\] \\[Signature Platform\\] |\n| :---- |\n\n**EXHIBIT 2 – MULTISIGNATURE SCHEME PROCESS**\n\n\\[\\]\n\n1. **Key Storage and Security**\n\nActive Signers are encouraged to implement robust security practices to safeguard their Keys and prevent unauthorized access. \n\nRecognizing the diverse approaches to key management, Active Signers have the flexibility to choose between hot or cold storage solutions for their Keys. The use of new hot wallets is permitted. However, for security best practices, the reuse of old wallets is not allowed. \n\nEach Active Signer will create their own unique wallet and utilize the corresponding Keys. The specific method of key storage and security implementation is left to the discretion of the individual Active Signer, who is expected to exercise due diligence in selecting a secure solution that aligns with their technical capabilities and risk tolerance.\n\n2. **Transaction** **Process**\n\n\\[\\]\n\n1. **Execution of a Decision**\n\nActive Signers are made aware of decisions of the Association in their capacity as Members. If they have not taken part in a specific decision, \\[…\\]\n\nIf an adopted decision does not sufficiently define all parameters of the transaction to be executed, the participants to the Multisignature Scheme shall review it in their capacity as Members before proceeding with its execution. \n\n2. **Signature Request Initiation**\n\nIf the Association has not specifically designated someone in the relevant decision to prepare the transaction and initiate the Signature Request, the Active Signer may take the initiative to do so. In such a case, the Active Signer shall share the Signature Request with all other participants in the Multisignature Scheme, accompanied by a communication specifying which decision the transaction is executing.\n\nSignature Requests will be made in English through the Multisignature Platform and include the following information for the accuracy of which the submitting Active Signer is responsible: \n\n* Token amount to be transferred \n\n* Token type to be transferred \n\n* Receiving address \n\n* Description of purpose for request (execution of association decision, agreement, invoice payment etc.)\n\nThe Active Signer must share the availability of the Signature Request on the Multisignature Platform with other participants of the Multisignature Scheme via the agreed private and secure communication as specified below (“**Channel**”).\n\n| Private Channel (for association members only) Discord channel  |\n| :---- |\n\n3. **Signature Request Response**\n\nThe Active Signer is expected to monitor the Channel regularly and must have enabled alerts/notifications to ensure each new Signature Request is read as soon as possible. If the Active Signer is unable to access the Channel or the Multisignature Platform to review a Signature Request, they must immediately inform the other participants to the Multisignature Scheme by appropriate means, including the reason for their inability to access. \n\nThe Active Signer shall decide whether to accept a Signature Request (i.e., to sign the relevant transaction message with the Key for broadcast to and processing on the relevant blockchain network) or reject it (i.e., refuse the relevant transaction message with the Key, thereby blocking it from further processing) within 48 hours from the receipt of a Signature Request, unless otherwise agreed in writing. \n\nUpon receiving a Signature Request emitted by another participant of the Multisignature Scheme, the Active Signer must review its content to ensure it aligns with its intended purpose. This may include verifying the information against relevant external documents (e.g., invoices, agreements, etc.), and must always include a review of all transaction-related addresses (i.e. recipient addresses or smart contract addresses) using *Diffchecker* (available at https://www.diffchecker.com/text-compare/) or similar. \n\nIf the Active Signer identifies any mistake, they must flag them on the Channel and recommend that the Signature Request be re-submitted on the Multisignature Platform. In such cases, the response deadline for the Signature Request is automatically extended by the time reasonably required to identify the correct information, re-enter the Signature Request and review the corrected Signature Request.\n\nIf necessary, the participant to the Multisignature Scheme may coordinate via the Channel, ask any relevant questions, and are expected to respond within a maximum of 24 hours. They should maintain open communication and a spirit of cooperation to foster positive relations with other Active Signers. When coordination is initiated, the Signature Request response deadline is extended by an additional 24 hours from the time the coordination request is posted on the Channel.\n\nIn the event of a dispute regarding the content of the Signature Request, the concerns raised by a participant to the Multisignature Scheme must be documented, analyzed, and discussed among all parties involved during the time deemed necessary but no longer than 72 hours. A Signature Request may be then approved if the Decision Quorum is reached, despite the presence of a dispute. \n\n4. **Transaction Failure**\n\nIn the event a signature request was approved but the transaction did not go through due to technical issues, the process outlined hereabove shall be repeated.\n\n5. **Recipient Confirmation** \n\nAfter the approved Signature Request has resulted in a successful transaction broadcasted to the relevant blockchain, the Participant of the Multisignature Scheme who initiated the Signature Request shall request a receipt confirmation from the recipient and share it on the Channel.\n\n**3\\. Amendment**\n\nOnce the Designated Ops Budget has been committed to the Wallet, the Parties shall not approve or cooperate with any replacement or modification of the Decision Quorum or the Multisignature Scheme except \n\n1) solely to the extent necessary to protect against a clear and present security threat; or  \n2) to facilitate removals, resignations and to fill vacancies. \n\nSubject to the foregoing limitations, the terms of this Exhibit shall be amended, supplemented, terminated or waived with the written consent of the majority of Active Signers. \n\n**4\\. Vacancy**\n\nIn the event of a vacancy that does not affect the ability to reach the Decision Quorum, the vacancy shall be remedied by the admission of a new Member within twenty (20) calendar days from the date the vacancy arises. A new Agreement shall be executed with the incoming Member as soon as reasonably practicable.\n\nIf a vacancy renders the Decision Quorum unachievable, this Agreement shall be deemed automatically terminated with respect to the remaining Participants in the Multisignature Scheme.\n\nIn such case of termination, control of the Wallet shall be temporarily attributed to a designated Member, as agreed by the remaining Members prior to termination, solely for the purpose of safeguarding assets and facilitating the transition to a new multisignature scheme. This designated Member shall not make any transactions from the Wallet except as expressly authorized by a duly adopted decision of the Association.\n\n3. \n\n   4. **Emergency Signature Requests**\n\n\\[…\\]\n\n3. **Amendment**\n\nOnce the Designated Ops Budget has been committed to the Wallet, the Parties shall not approve or cooperate with any replacement or modification of the Decision Quorum or the Multisignature Scheme except \n\n3) solely to the extent necessary to protect against a clear and present security threat; or  \n4) to facilitate removals, resignations and to fill vacancies. \n\nSubject to the foregoing limitations, the terms of this Exhibit shall be amended, supplemented, terminated or waived with the written consent of the majority of Active Signers.\n\n4. **Security**\n\n\\[Cold storage details and expected precautions for key conservation and use\\] \n\n5. **Vacancy**\n\n\\[…\\]\n\n**Exhibit 3 – LIST OF INTERNAL POLICIES** \n\nFinance Control Policy\n\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1ecBRhD0TolpeD7zAXUeOtThZtPwSrZdsVK2pgtRcblM/edit?tab=t.0\\#heading=h.8rspsnpqlny2\n\n";

export const regulationGATemplateRaw = "\n\n**Regulations general Assembly**\n\n**Swiss Association** \n\n**Description:**\n\nDecision- making rules and Procedure of General Assembly (main governing body of the Swiss Association\n\n**Variable Parameters**\n\n* *Association Name:* Legal title of your association  \n* *Signatories (Name, Entity, Role)*  \n* *Date (Day, Month , Year)*\n\n**Fix Parameters**\n\n* *Role (Chair)*  \n* *Default majority rule: (absolute majority)*  \n* *Special majority rule (unanimous)*\n\n\n  **\\[Association Name\\] Regulation General Assembly** \n\n**Article I. Purpose and application** \n\nThis Regulation General Assembly (**“Regulation GA”**) is adopted by the General Assembly of the \n\n**\\[Association Name\\]** association (**“Association\"**) and governs \n\ntogether with the applicable laws, the **\\[Association Name\\]**  articles of association (as \n\namended, the **\"Articles\"**), and other regulations (if any), the organization of the Association. \n\nIn case of any conflict or inconsistency between the applicable laws, the Regulation GA, Articles or the \n\nan other regulation, the following order of precedence shall govern: (1) mandatory applicable laws, (2) \n\nthe Articles and this Regulation GA (the more specific shall prevail), (3) the other regulations. In case of \n\nany conflict or inconsistency between the other regulations or organizational documents, the one relating \n\nto the subject matter shall prevail. \n\n**Article II. Definitions** \n\nTerms not otherwise defined in the Regulation GA shall have the meaning assigned to them in the \n\nArticles or any other regulation of the Association. \n\n**\"Chair**\" means the person elected by the General Assembly as chair, or, in the case of his inability, \n\nanother Member attending the General Assembly. \n\n**\"General Assembly**\" means the meeting of the Members of the Association and the resolutions by means of written/electronic means *(Urabstimmung*). \n\n**\"Member**\" means a member of the Association as defined in the Articles. \n\n**\"Chair**\" means the member of the Board elected by the other members of the Board to preside over the \n\nBoard. \n\n**Article III. General Membership Criteria** \n\nApplicants for membership in the Association must meet the following criteria: \n\na. legally valid status as a party to a \"Multisignature Participation Agreement\" pertaining to a \n\nmultisignature cryptocurrency wallet which is administered for the purpose of the Association as stated in Article 3 of the Articles. \n\nb. be a natural person (or persons), a decentralized unincorporated organization or an AI application \n\nin the Web3 industry represented by one or more natural or legal persons, corporation, partnership, association, trust, public or private non-profit research institution, governmental body, or other legal entity; \n\nc. willingness to support and work toward the purpose of the Association; \n\nd. good reputation; \n\ne. good standing; and \n\nf. no increased reputational, financial, or criminal risk for the Association by admitting the applicant. \n\n**Article IV. General Assembly** \n\n1\\. **Convening and holding the General Assembly** \n\nThe virtual or physical General Assembly will take place upon invitation by the Chair, or by request of a \n\nMember. The notice can be made electronically (e-mail or other means of communication) or in writing and \n\nshall state the place (if not a virtual assembly) and/or the access information (if a virtual assembly) and time \n\nof the meeting, the items of the agenda as well as the motions for consideration, if any. Meetings must be \n\ncalled at least five (5) days in advance. \n\nAlternative motions by Members for the agenda can be sent to the Chair within two (2) days after dispatch or \n\npublishing of the invitation notice with or without a reasoning. The Chair shall publish the alternative \n\nmotions and any reasonings at least one (1) before the virtual or physical General Assembly. \n\nNo later than ten (10) days prior to the day of the ordinary General Assembly (as set out in the notice calling \n\nthe General Assembly), the financial statements of the Association and the report issued by the auditors shall \n\nbe made available to the Members for inspection either at the registered office of the Association or online. \n\nIf no objection is raised by any Member, the Members may hold a General Assembly without observing the \n\nprescribed formalities of calling the meeting. \n\nThe General Assembly will be chaired by the Chair or, in the case of his inability, another member of the \n\nBoard attending the General Assembly. \n\n2\\. **Organisation of written/electronic resolutions (\"Urabstimmungen\")** \n\nVoting by written / electronic means (Urabstimmung) takes place upon determination by the Members and \n\ninvitation by the Chair. The voting window shall be five (5) days and the deadline for submitting votes shall be communicated in the invitation. \n\nThe invitation to participate in the written/ electronic voting has to be sent out or published at least five (5) days before the start of the voting window and can be made electronically (communication by mail, e-mail, or any other means of communication) or in writing. It shall include the items on which resolutions shall be taken as well as the motions as determined by the Board. \n\nIn the case of a written / electronic voting (Urabstimmung) in lieu of an ordinary General Assembly the \n\nfinancial statements of the Association as well as the report issued by the auditors have to be disclosed online at the same time as the invitation is sent out by the Chair \n\nAlternative motions can be sent to the Board within two (2) days after dispatch or publishing of the voting material with or without reasoning. The Board shall publish the alternative motions and any reasonings at east one (1) day before the voting window starts together with the final voting material which allows the Members to vote on all motions received. \n\n3\\. **Voting rights** \n\nEach Member has one vote at the General Assembly and for the written/ electronic voting (*Urabstimmung*). \n\nVotes are not transferable to another member or a third person. \n\n4\\. **Majority requirements** \n\nUnless otherwise required by law or the Articles, resolutions shall be passed, and elections shall be made by the \\[default majority rule \\=absolute majority\\]  of all votes cast at the General Assembly. \n\nThe Chair of the meeting will not have the casting vote. \n\nThe majorities for decisions of the General Assembly shall apply likewise to decisions taken by written / electronic communication *(Urabstimmung*). \n\nA Member and its Affiliates will be deemed as one (1) Member for all Association votes and quorum calculations. **\"Affiliate\"** or **\"Affiliates\"** means any entity that is controlled by, under common control with, or that controls the subject party; and 'control' means direct or indirect control of more than fifty (50) % of the voting power to elect directors of an entity or, for any other entity, the power to direct management of such entity. \n\nAny amendment of the Articles or these Regulations GA requires a \\[special majority rule \\= unanimous vote\\] by all Members. \n\n**Article V. Modifications** \n\nThe General Assembly may modify or amend any rule(s) in the Regulation GA at any time within the \n\npurpose of the Association for good governance, subject to any limitation in the Articles or any regulation. \n\nApproved by the General Assembly on \\[Date\\]\n\n**Signatory 1 (Role \\= chair\\]**\n\n**Signatory 2 (Role \\= secretary)**\n\n";

export const dissolutionResolutionTemplateRaw = "**General Assembly Resolution**\n\n**Dissolution and Liquidation of [Association Name]**\n\nDate: [Date]\nForm: [Form]\n\n## 1. Dissolution\n\nThe Association is dissolved with immediate effect.\n\n## 2. Confirmation of Financial Status\n\nThe Members confirm no outstanding debts or obligations.\n\n## 3. Liquidation Execution\n\nMembers shall execute liquidation, including asset transfers and transactions.\n\n## 4. Asset Allocation\n\nRemaining assets shall be allocated as follows:\n\n[Insert recipient]\n\nThe allocation:\n- aligns with the Association's purpose;\n- does not benefit Members or related parties.\n\n## 5. Completion\n\nUpon execution of transfers, liquidation is complete.\n\n## 6. Formal Closure\n\nWhere applicable:\n- deregister from Swiss Commercial Register;\n- retain records.\n\n## Confirmation\n\nThis resolution is adopted unanimously.\n\n## Signatures\n\n[Signatures]\n";

